   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "JKz7wQRzjvR89dXrThdsP6",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "My lifelong commitment to service, social justice and fairness for all inspired me to enter politics, so I could make a difference in people's lives. After several terms, I still have the energy and passion to do more. I find being an electorate MP and assisting constituents is very important and rewarding work. As an MP, I can influence policy and make laws that change frameworks and systems and uplift people's lives."
     },
     {
      "_key": "JKz7wQRzjvR89dXrThdsSL",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "My upbringing celebrated service and hard work. Inspired by my family's deep commitment to church and community, I pursued a career in public service and community volunteering before becoming an MP. I would continue to bring the same work ethic and passion to serve to my role as MP for Ōtāhuhu. In Parliament, I would bring my legal and policy skills plus political expertise to bear on policy development and beneficial laws for all."
     },
     {
      "_key": "JKz7wQRzjvR89dXrThdsVa",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Get the cost of living crisis under control. We will tackle costs, grow jobs & support business."
     },
     {
      "_key": "JKz7wQRzjvR89dXrThdsYp",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Fix housing. Good quality homes underpin health, people's ability to work & children's education."
     },
     {
      "_key": "JKz7wQRzjvR89dXrThdsc4",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Ensure the healthcare people need. They must be able to see a GP, afford medicine & access hospitals."
     }
    ],
